# Components & pages

## Thin pages

Pages only mount a feature entry — put UI in `components/pages/<feature>/`:

```vue
<!-- ✅ app/pages/index.vue -->
<template>
  <UserReservationsPageIndex />
</template>
<script setup>
import UserReservationsPageIndex from "~/components/pages/user-reservations/UserReservationsPageIndex.vue";
definePageMeta({ layout: "public" });
</script>
```

## Naming

| Kind | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| Shared reusable | kebab folder + `index.vue` | [`shared/dialog/reservation-success-dialog/`](mdc:app/components/shared/dialog/reservation-success-dialog/index.vue) |
| Feature page shell | PascalCase `*PageIndex.vue` | `UsersPageIndex.vue` |
| Feature form/table/dialog | PascalCase `.vue` under feature tree | `UserForm.vue`, `SalesSuccessDialog.vue` |

## Script patterns

- Always `<script setup>` (no Options API components)
- Prefer `defineOptions({ name: "PascalCaseName" })` (common on shared; not universal)
- Dialogs: `visible` prop + `update:visible` / `close` emits
- Import PrimeVue pieces explicitly (`Dialog`, `Button`, …)
- Style with **Tailwind** first; scoped CSS only when needed (see `app-data-table`)

## Placement

- Reusable across features → [`app/components/shared/`](mdc:app/components/shared/) (usually kebab + `index.vue`; some report shells use PascalCase folders e.g. `ReportsSummaryCards/`)
- Feature-only → [`app/components/pages/<feature>/`](mdc:app/components/pages/user-reservations/)
- Layout chrome → [`app/layouts/`](mdc:app/layouts/)
- [`app/pages/index.vue`](mdc:app/pages/index.vue) mounts `UserReservationsPageIndex`

